      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2026,
      "shift": "2 Apr 2026, Shift 2",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "The number of points in the interval [2,4], at which the function $f(x) = \\left[ x^2 - x - \\; \\frac{1}{2} \\right]$, where $[\\cdot]$ denotes the greatest integer function, is discontinuous, is _____ .",
      "image": null,
      "options": [],
      "answer": {
        "min": 10.0,
        "max": 10.0
      },
      "solution": "**Key idea:** $[g(x)]$ is discontinuous exactly where the continuous function $g(x)$ passes through an integer value. The endpoints need a separate check.\nLet $g(x) = x^2 - x - \\frac{1}{2}$.\n$g'(x) = 2x - 1 > 0$ for $x \\in [2,4]$, so $g$ is strictly increasing on $[2,4]$.\n$g(2) = 4 - 2 - \\frac{1}{2} = 1.5$\n$g(4) = 16 - 4 - \\frac{1}{2} = 11.5$\nSo $g$ increases continuously from $1.5$ to $11.5$. It passes through each integer $2, 3, \\dots, 11$ exactly once, at an interior point of the interval.\nAt each such point, $[g(x)]$ jumps by $1$, so $f$ is discontinuous there. This gives $11 - 2 + 1 = 10$ points.\nAt the endpoints, $g(2) = 1.5$ and $g(4) = 11.5$ are not integers. So $f$ is continuous at $x = 2$ and $x = 4$.\nTotal number of points of discontinuity $= 10$.\nAnswer: 10"
    },
